  "evidence": "SwissWatchExpo 59483 original specimen. All 12 original gallery images inspected 17 November 2026; movement 8 reviewed at 1200px from original 1751px file. Visible 3135 bridge stamp and THIRTY-ONE 31 inscription. Case engraving 6 visibly 16618; listing matches exact reference. Blue dial with visible colour variation, blue bezel and yellow-metal Oyster/flip-lock visible. Dealer attributes 1991–1992, 40mm 18k yellow-gold case/bracelet and sapphire crystal; these remain attributions, not material assay or independent chronology. Dealer calls dial unique patina; cause, originality and luminous composition cannot be established from these photographs. No black-dial, Serti or later ceramic execution transfer. No transfer to neighbouring references or other unopened specimens; original fitment, service status, full chronology and user-watch authenticity are not independently established. Existing photographs remain separate specimens. Overall execution/period research remains incomplete.",
